.gsd/milestones/M001/slices/S05/S05-SUMMARY.md:51:**S05 created the final documentation-UAT/release-gate evidence trail and verified mechanics, while honestly leaving human UAT and `/deep-review` unresolved in auto-mode.**
.gsd/milestones/M001/slices/S05/S05-SUMMARY.md:55:S05 consumed S04's README/SECURITY/TODO remediation and converted it into a durable release-validation packet. The slice added `S05-DOCS-REVIEW-PACKET.md`, which tells a human operator/release reviewer to inspect the committed `a3f09ad^..HEAD` documentation range for portable config-directory behavior, Docker versus standalone first-run behavior, nested multi-instance TOML examples, auth/security modes, External-auth direct-access blocking, ASGI/Uvicorn secure-cookie trust boundaries, and TODO retirement. It then added `S05-UAT-GATE.md`, which records the key truth for downstream validation: auto-mode had no human approval, change request, or explicit deferral, so the documentation UAT gate is unresolved and human UAT has not passed. The same artifact records `/deep-review` as blocked/unavailable rather than completed or human-deferred.
.gsd/milestones/M001/slices/S05/S05-SUMMARY.md:57:T03 added and the closer refreshed `S05-RELEASE-GATE-EVIDENCE.md` as a blocked-gate evidence index. Mechanical checks passed, but the index explicitly recommends milestone validation `needs-attention`, not `pass`, because release readiness depends on a human documentation decision and the `/deep-review` release decision. No runtime code or production wiring changed. The pattern established by this slice is the separation of human acceptance from agent diagnostics: review packets and tests can prepare evidence, but only a real human decision can move the gate out of unresolved. `.gsd/PROJECT.md` was also refreshed so future agents see that S05 produced evidence but did not resolve the human/release gate.
.gsd/milestones/M001/slices/S05/S05-SUMMARY.md:69:Important result: mechanical verification passes, but human UAT is not approved; the correct milestone validation posture is needs-attention until a human resolves the gate.
.gsd/milestones/M001/slices/S05/S05-SUMMARY.md:97:Human documentation UAT remains unresolved, and `/deep-review` has not been run or explicitly deferred by a human. Therefore release readiness is blocked and milestone validation should be needs-attention despite passing mechanical verification.
.gsd/milestones/M001/slices/S05/S05-SUMMARY.md:101:A human must review the README/SECURITY/TODO diff range `a3f09ad^..HEAD` using the S05 review packet and record approval, approval with caveats, changes requested, or explicit deferral. Before push/tag/release, a human should run `/deep-review` or explicitly defer it with scope and rationale.
.gsd/milestones/M001/slices/S05/S05-SUMMARY.md:106:- `.gsd/milestones/M001/slices/S05/S05-UAT-GATE.md` — Gate record showing human documentation UAT and `/deep-review` are unresolved in auto-mode.
.gsd/milestones/M001/slices/S05/S05-SUMMARY.md:107:- `.gsd/milestones/M001/slices/S05/S05-RELEASE-GATE-EVIDENCE.md` — Blocked-gate evidence index with fresh mechanical verification command artifacts and needs-attention recommendation.
